Third-party software under the GNU LGPL
---------------------------------------

Rufi shows HEIC photos through heic-decode (ISC licence), which includes
libheif-js 1.23.5: libheif 1.23 and its HEVC decoder libde265 1.0.15,
built to WebAssembly. libheif and libde265 are licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 3 (LGPL-3.0). Their licence texts,
with the GNU General Public License, version 3, that the LGPL refers to,
are in licenses/libheif.txt.

- libheif: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif (the 1.23 release that
  libheif-js 1.23.5's install script names)
- libde265: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265 (tag v1.0.15)
- libheif-js, the WebAssembly build: https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js
  (tag v1.23.5)

Rufi doesn't change these libraries. They stay their own package
(node_modules/libheif-js), outside Rufi's code, loaded at run time, so you
can replace them with another build of the same interface: put your build
in that package's place, keeping its file names.

